that consciousness is simply an emergent property the brain produces, something like software running

00:09:26.470 --> 00:09:32.270
on neural hardware. Yet, Kristoff Koch's recent reflections push against that comfortable picture by

00:09:32.270 --> 00:09:37.770
insisting we confront what philosophers call the hard problem. Why does any of this information

00:09:37.770 --> 00:09:43.530
process income with subjective experience at all? Why isn't it all just dark inside like a sophisticated

